    "q-35285": {
      "dom_id": "step-q35285",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "If \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -9 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}]$, then $\\text{rank}(A)=$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the rank of $A,$ we first reduce it to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -6 & -9 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $2$ pivot columns (or alternatively, it has exactly $2$ non-zero rows).\n\nTherefore, $\\text{rank}(A)=2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
